{"cmd":"add","id":"node_readme","type":"card","group":"group_project","data":{"title":"LATAM Growth Dashboard — Product Overview (README)","description":"Single source of truth for the think4ever LATAM market launch, built and owned by the Research team. It unifies landing-page traffic, sign-ups, platform account creation, social and paid media performance into one dashboard so Research, Marketing and Growth leads stop switching between HubSpot, GA4, PostHog, Meta, LinkedIn, Google Ads and Clarity. Defines five views (Overview, Acquisition, Conversion, Social and paid, Data sources), four data-entry paths (seed JSON, scheduled connectors, CSV import, POST api/ingest), the service variables each source needs, and the Think4Ever deployment procedure (zip upload, `node server.js`, health check on /api/health). Business rules: launch date defaults to 2026-10-01, internal domain defaults to think4ever.com (used to flag internal test sign-ups), credentials live only in service variables and never in files.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","domain:latam-launch","role:research","role:marketing","entity:metric","entity:source","tech:documentation"],"sourceFiles":["README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ingest_engine","type":"card","group":"group_ingestion","data":{"title":"Ingest Engine (single load format)","description":"The heart of the dashboard's data layer: one function ingest(payload, how) that applies any data load — seed files, CSV import, scheduled connectors, 'Sync now' and POST api/ingest — to the store using one unified format { source, pulled_at, from, to, metrics, snapshots, events, notes, status }. This lets Research and Growth combine HubSpot, GA4, PostHog, Meta, Clarity, LinkedIn exports and manual research notes into one LATAM launch view without per-source code paths. Business rules: source must match /^[a-z0-9_]{2,30}$/ (else 400 'source missing or invalid'); metrics need ISO date, a metric name and a finite numeric value, otherwise silently skipped; snapshots need key + valid from/to; strings are truncated (metric 60, dim 40, dim_value 120, snapshot note 300, note label 140) and snapshot rows capped at 500, events at 5000. Metrics are upserted by key source|metric|date|dim|dim_value (idempotent re-loads overwrite daily facts); snapshots upserted by source|key|from|to; events REPLACE all of that source's events within [from,to] (delete-then-insert, so re-pulls never duplicate sign-ups); notes upserted by id or date-source-slug(label). After every load it marks the source status (state default 'connected', note, last_sync, window 'from to to') and appends a synclog entry {source, at, how, metrics, snapshots, events} used by the Data sources 'load history'.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","role:research-analyst","role:integration-client","entity:metric","entity:snapshot","entity:event","entity:note","entity:source-status","entity:synclog","flow:data-load","tech:node"],"sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_package","type":"card","group":"group_project","data":{"title":"package.json — t4e-growth-dashboard","description":"Node package manifest for the dashboard service (v1.0.0, private). Declares the runtime contract: Node >= 18 (needed for native fetch used by connectors), entry point server.js, start script `node server.js`. Only three dependencies keep the deployment small: express (HTTP API and static UI), mysql2 (persistence in the Think4Ever MySQL add-on) and dotenv (local .env loading). The description positions the product as 'one place for HubSpot, Google Analytics, PostHog, Clarity, Meta and LinkedIn data'.","tags":["domain:deployment","tech:nodejs","tech:express","tech:mysql2","tech:dotenv"],"sourceFiles":["package.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_server_bootstrap","type":"card","group":"group_project","data":{"title":"Server Bootstrap & Lifecycle (server.js)","description":"Boots the growth dashboard service. Loads env via dotenv, mounts JSON body parsing (2 MB limit to allow large CSV/API loads) and serves the static dashboard from /public. On start it initializes the store (creates gd_items table in MySQL or falls back to data/local.json), runs the seed loader for any source without data (HubSpot and GA4, 1–14 Oct 2026), then listens on process.env.PORT. Business rule: PORT is mandatory — the Think4Ever runtime must inject it; the process exits with code 1 otherwise, and also exits if boot fails. Schedules the first automatic connector sync 20 seconds after boot and then every 6 hours. A final error middleware hides internals and returns 500 {error:'internal error'}.","tags":["domain:deployment","domain:data-ingestion","tech:express","tech:nodejs","integration:mysql","state:boot"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_ingest","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"POST","path":"/api/ingest","description":"Universal data-load endpoint used by Research scripts, the CSV import in the Data sources view, and conceptually by connectors. Accepts a payload for one source and window, delegates normalization/upsert to lib/ingest, which records a load in the sync log. Header x-load-how: csv marks loads coming from the CSV importer; everything else is tagged 'api'. Validation errors thrown by ingest with a status are returned with that status.","params":[{"name":"source","type":"string","required":true},{"name":"from","type":"date YYYY-MM-DD","required":false},{"name":"to","type":"date YYYY-MM-DD","required":false},{"name":"metrics","type":"array<{date,metric,value,dim?,dim_value?}>","required":false},{"name":"snapshots","type":"array<{key,from,to,rows}>","required":false},{"name":"events","type":"array","required":false},{"name":"notes","type":"array","required":false},{"name":"x-ingest-key","type":"header","required":false},{"name":"x-load-how","type":"header ('csv')","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"ingest summary (e.g. { metrics: n, events: n, ... }); 401 { error: 'ingest key' }; 4xx { error } on validation; 500 internal error"},"auth":"team-code (if set) + x-ingest-key (if INGEST_KEY set)","sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_env_config","type":"card","group":"group_project","data":{"title":"Service Variables (Environment Configuration)","description":"All credentials and behavior switches come from Think4Ever service variables, never from files. Per source: HUBSPOT_TOKEN (private app with contacts read, forms, business-intelligence scopes); GA4_PROPERTY_ID + GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT (service-account key JSON with Viewer access); POSTHOG_HOST, POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID, POSTHOG_API_KEY; META_TOKEN + META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID; CLARITY_TOKEN. Optional: TEAM_CODE (shared code gate on /api), INGEST_KEY (protects ingest), LAUNCH_DATE (default 2026-10-01), INTERNAL_DOMAINS (default think4ever.com), DATABASE_URL or DB_* for MySQL, PORT (required). A connector is considered 'configured' (auto sync enabled) only when all its variables are present.","tags":["domain:configuration","domain:security","role:operator","tech:env-vars","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","integration:posthog","integration:meta","integration:clarity"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed_loader","type":"card","group":"group_ingestion","data":{"title":"First-Boot Seed Loader","description":"Guarantees the dashboard is never empty on a fresh deployment: on boot it reads every seed/*.json file (alphabetical: ga4, hubspot, posthog, research) and ingests it with how='seed' — but only for sources that have no synclog entry yet. Once a source has been loaded by any path (seed, connector, CSV, API) its seed is never re-applied, so live data is never overwritten by the baseline snapshot. Returns the number of seed files applied; silently does nothing if the seed directory is missing.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","flow:first-boot-seed","entity:synclog","tech:filesystem"],"sourceFiles":["lib/seed.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_team_code_gate","type":"card","group":"group_access","data":{"title":"Team Code Gate (/api middleware)","description":"Lightweight shared-secret access control for the whole dashboard API. When TEAM_CODE is set, every /api request (except the health check, which is registered before the middleware) must carry header x-team-code equal to it; otherwise the server returns 401 {error:'code'}. When TEAM_CODE is empty the API is open. On the client, a 401 with error 'code' triggers the Team code prompt ('Ask the Research lead for it'); the code is saved in localStorage key 't4e-growth-code' and sent on every subsequent fetch. Security notes: single shared code (no per-user identity or roles), plain string comparison, stored client-side in localStorage — suitable for internal team obscurity, not strong authentication.","tags":["domain:security","role:team-member","role:research-lead","tech:express-middleware","entity:team-code"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_data_load","type":"note","group":"group_ingestion","data":{"text":"**Flow: Data load (any origin)**\n1. A load arrives from: seed file, CSV import (date, metric, value[, dim, dim_value]), scheduled connector (every 6h), 'Sync now', or POST api/ingest\n2. Validate source id; reject with 400 if invalid\n3. Upsert each valid metric (daily fact) keyed source|metric|date|dim|dim_value\n4. Upsert each snapshot (window table) keyed source|key|from|to, stamping pulled_at\n5. If events + from/to provided: delete this source's events in window, insert new ones (max 5000)\n6. Upsert timeline notes (shown on Overview daily sessions chart)\n7. Update source status: state (default connected), note, last_sync, window\n8. Write synclog {source, at, how, counts} → Data sources load history\n\n**Roles:** Research analyst, automation, scheduler\n**Rules:** invalid rows skipped silently; strings truncated; idempotent re-loads\n**Errors:** 400 invalid source; DB errors propagate to caller","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ingest_key","type":"card","group":"group_access","data":{"title":"Ingest Key Protection","description":"Second, optional secret dedicated to write access for data loads. When INGEST_KEY is set, POST /api/ingest requires header x-ingest-key matching it, else 401 {error:'ingest key'}. This lets external scripts (Research automations) push data without exposing the team code, and lets operators lock down writes separately from reads. It stacks with the TEAM_CODE gate (both apply when both are set). Connector syncs triggered internally bypass HTTP and call ingest directly.","tags":["domain:security","domain:data-ingestion","role:research","role:automation","entity:ingest-key"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_first_boot","type":"note","group":"group_ingestion","data":{"text":"**Flow: First boot seeding**\n1. Server starts, store.init() creates gd_items (or loads data/local.json)\n2. seed() lists synclog → set of sources already loaded\n3. For each seed/*.json (sorted) whose source is not in the set → ingest(p,'seed')\n4. Baseline 1–14 Oct 2026 appears for HubSpot, GA4, PostHog and Research readings\n\n**Rule:** seed never overwrites a source that already has any load history","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["lib/seed.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_security_notes","type":"note","group":"group_access","data":{"text":"**Security posture summary**\n- Read access: optional TEAM_CODE header gate on /api (shared code, localStorage on client).\n- Write access to data: optional INGEST_KEY on /api/ingest.\n- Health endpoints (/health, /api/health) are always public for the platform health check.\n- Input validation: note date regex YYYY-MM-DD, label ≤140 chars, note kind whitelist; source state whitelist, source note ≤300 chars; unknown source keys → 404.\n- XSS: frontend escapes all dynamic strings with esc() before injecting HTML.\n- Errors: generic 500 'internal error'; connector errors truncated to 300 chars.\n- Credentials only in service variables; seeds/data folder excluded from upload zip.\n- No per-user auth, no CSRF tokens (API uses custom headers + JSON, which limits simple CSRF).","color":"#FBEAEA","sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_connector_registry","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"Connector Registry & Configuration Gate","description":"Server-side pull connectors for HubSpot, GA4, PostHog, Meta Ads and Clarity. Each returns a load in the ingest format covering the launch window LAUNCH_DATE (default 2026-10-01) to today. REQUIRED maps each connector to its service variables and configured(key) returns true only when all are set, so the 6-hourly scheduler and 'Sync now' skip unconfigured sources instead of failing. Security & privacy rules: credentials only live in environment/service variables, never in files or DB; contact emails are reduced to their domain and classified internal/external using INTERNAL_DOMAINS (default think4ever.com) so internal test sign-ups can be excluded from growth figures. Shared http() helper throws '<status> <first 200 chars>' on non-2xx, which the caller surfaces as a sync error.","tags":["domain:integrations","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","integration:posthog","integration:meta-ads","integration:clarity","flow:scheduled-sync","role:system-scheduler"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_health","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/api/health (alias /health)","description":"Platform health check used by Think4Ever after deploy. Pings the store (MySQL or local JSON) and reports which backend is active. Registered before the team-code middleware so it is always reachable without credentials.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ status: 'ok', store: 'mysql' | 'local' }; 503 { status: 'error', error } when the store ping fails"},"auth":"public","sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_data","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/api/data","description":"The single read endpoint powering every dashboard view. Returns the full growth dataset and the browser aggregates it client-side by period. Strips internal _at timestamps from rows. Sources are merged from the static catalog (lib/sources) with live state stored in the DB plus an 'auto' flag telling whether the connector is configured. Sync log is limited to the last 30 entries, newest first.","params":[{"name":"x-team-code","type":"header","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ generated_at, metrics[{source,metric,date,value,dim,dim_value}], snapshots[{source,key,from,to,rows}], events[{kind,date,internal,...}], notes[{id,date,label,kind}], sources[{key,name,area,provides,connect,env,state,note,last_sync,window,auto}], synclog[{source,at,how,error?,...}] }"},"auth":"team-code (if TEAM_CODE set)","sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_conn_hubspot","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"HubSpot Connector (landing traffic + sign-up log)","description":"Pulls daily landing analytics by traffic source from /analytics/v2/reports/sources/daily and maps HubSpot visits/visitors/rawViews/bounces/contacts to metrics sessions/new_visitors/pageviews/bounces/contacts with dim 'source' (labels: Direct, Email, Other campaigns, Paid search, Paid social, Referrals, Organic social, Organic search, Offline). Then pages through CRM contact search (createdate ≥ launch 05:00 UTC, i.e. Colombia midnight; 100 per page) to build the sign-up log: events kind 'form_signup' with date, form (last part of recent_conversion_event_name), source, country (country or ip_country), internal flag and domain_type none/internal/external. No email or name is stored — only the domain classification. Feeds the Acquisition 'Sessions by source' and Conversion 'sign-up log' views.","tags":["integration:hubspot","domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","entity:contact","entity:form-signup","entity:session","security:pii-minimisation"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_conn_ga4","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"Google Analytics 4 Connector","description":"Authenticates with a service account by building and RS256-signing a JWT locally (analytics.readonly scope) and exchanging it at oauth2.googleapis.com for an access token — no Google SDK dependency. Runs Data API runReport queries for the launch window: date×sessionDefaultChannelGroup → ga_sessions/ga_engaged_sessions/ga_users by channel; date×eventName → ga_event by event (form_start, sign_up, login, generate_lead defined via Tag Manager); country snapshot (users, engaged_sessions, key_events); and a totals snapshot (users, new users, sessions, engaged sessions, engagement rate, pageviews, events, key events). Feeds Acquisition channels/countries and Conversion landing events.","tags":["integration:ga4","integration:google-oauth","domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","entity:channel","entity:landing-event","tech:jwt"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_conn_posthog","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"PostHog Connector (platform accounts)","description":"Queries the think4ever platform's PostHog project via HogQL to measure what happens after the landing: daily custom events (excluding $-prefixed autocaptured events) as ph_event by event, daily distinct active people as ph_active_users, and daily new persons as ph_new_persons. This is the bottom of the funnel — accounts actually created and activated in the platform — used for 'Platform sign-ups' in Conversion and the funnel's active-account step. Note: dates are interpolated into SQL from LAUNCH_DATE (server-controlled env, not user input).","tags":["integration:posthog","domain:activation","entity:person","entity:platform-event","flow:funnel"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_sync","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"POST","path":"/api/sync/:source","description":"'Sync now' button backend. Runs the automatic connector for one source immediately and ingests the result tagged 'connector'. Business rules: only sources with a connector (hubspot, ga4, posthog, meta, clarity) can sync; the connector must be configured with all its service variables. On connector failure the error is written to the sync log (key '<iso>|<source>', how 'connector', error ≤300 chars) so the Data sources load history shows it.","params":[{"name":"source","type":"path string","required":true}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"ingest summary; 404 { error: 'No automatic connector for this source' }; 409 { error: 'Service variables for this source are not set yet' }; 502 { error } when the upstream API fails"},"auth":"team-code (if TEAM_CODE set)","sourceFiles":["server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_conn_meta","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"Meta Ads Connector","description":"Pulls Facebook/Instagram ad insights at campaign level, one row per day (Graph API v19.0, paginated 500 per page) and stores ad_spend, ad_impressions, ad_clicks and ad_results (sum of actions matching lead or complete_registration) by campaign. Enables the Social and paid view and cost per sign-up once paid campaigns run. Accepts the ad account id with or without 'act_' prefix. Token passed as query parameter, URL-encoded.","tags":["integration:meta-ads","domain:paid-media","entity:campaign","entity:ad-spend","flow:cost-per-signup"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_sources_put","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"PUT","path":"/api/sources/:key","description":"Lets the Research team manually track the onboarding status of each data source (e.g. LinkedIn or Google Ads access still pending) from the Data sources view. Merges with any previously stored state. Business rules: key must exist in the source catalog; state only accepted if one of connected | pending | not_started; note truncated to 300 chars; other fields ignored.","params":[{"name":"key","type":"path string","required":true},{"name":"state","type":"'connected'|'pending'|'not_started'","required":false},{"name":"note","type":"string ≤300","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ state?, note?, last_sync?, window? } stored source record; 404 { error: 'source' }"},"auth":"team-code (if TEAM_CODE set)","sourceFiles":["server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_conn_clarity","type":"card","group":"group_connectors","data":{"title":"Microsoft Clarity Connector","description":"Calls Clarity's project-live-insights export (last 3 days — the API's limit) and stores a single 'live_insights' snapshot (max 200 rows of metricName + information) for the last-3-days window. Gives UX signals on the landing: scroll depth, rage/dead clicks, traffic origin. No daily metrics are produced because Clarity only exposes rolling windows.","tags":["integration:clarity","domain:landing-ux","entity:snapshot"],"sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_notes_post","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"POST","path":"/api/notes","description":"Adds a timeline annotation (campaign launch, social post, landing fix, test) that appears as numbered orange markers on the Overview daily sessions chart, helping explain traffic spikes. Rules: date must match YYYY-MM-DD and label is required; label truncated to 140 chars; kind whitelisted to launch|content|fix|test|other (defaults to other); id = '<date>-<timestamp>'.","params":[{"name":"date","type":"YYYY-MM-DD","required":true},{"name":"label","type":"string ≤140","required":true},{"name":"kind","type":"launch|content|fix|test|other","required":false}],"response":{"status":201,"body":"{ id, date, label, kind }; 400 { error: 'date and label are required' }"},"auth":"team-code (if TEAM_CODE set)","sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_notes_delete","type":"api","group":"group_api","data":{"method":"DELETE","path":"/api/notes/:id","description":"Removes a timeline note (e.g. a mistaken annotation) from the store.","params":[{"name":"id","type":"path string","required":true}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ ok: true }; 404 { error: 'not found' }"},"auth":"team-code (if TEAM_CODE set)","sourceFiles":["server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_scheduled_sync","type":"note","group":"group_connectors","data":{"text":"**Flow: Connector sync (every 6h or 'Sync now')**\n1. For each connector key, configured(key) checks REQUIRED env vars\n2. Unconfigured → skipped (source stays pending/not_started in catalog)\n3. Connector authenticates (Bearer token / signed JWT / access_token param)\n4. Pulls LAUNCH_DATE..today (Clarity: last 3 days)\n5. Normalises to {source, from, to, metrics, snapshots, events}\n6. ingest(load,'connector') → store + status 'connected' + synclog\n\n**Errors:** http() throws '<status> <body excerpt>' → reported for that source; others continue\n**Security:** secrets only in service variables; emails → domain only; internal domains flagged","color":"#f3e8ff","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_sources_view","type":"card","group":"group_api","data":{"title":"Source Status Composer (sourcesView)","description":"Builds the Data sources status list by combining the static catalog (lib/sources: key, name, area, provides, connect instructions, env variables, default state/note) with live overrides from stored 'source' records (state, note, last_sync, window) and the configured() flag for automatic sync. This drives the status pills (Connected / Access pending / Not started), the source tags on every KPI and the empty-state messages that explain why a chart has no data yet.","tags":["domain:data-sources","entity:source","role:research"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_source_catalog","type":"card","group":"group_catalog","data":{"title":"Data Source Catalog","description":"Static, business-facing catalog of every data source the LATAM growth team relies on, rendered in the Data sources view: key, display name, business area (Landing and CRM, Landing behaviour, Event definitions, Platform, Social and paid, Paid), what it provides, required service variables, step-by-step connection instructions and a default state/note. Live state stored under kind 'source' (written by ingest) overrides state and note, so the catalog documents intent while the store reflects reality. Sources: HubSpot (connected), Google Analytics 4 (connected), Google Tag Manager (connected, documentation-only — defines GA events), PostHog (pending until baseline), Microsoft Clarity (pending), Meta (pending, CSV fallback), LinkedIn (pending, CSV export only), Google Ads (not_started; costs will flow through GA4). Guarantees every metric in the dashboard has a documented origin.","tags":["domain:data-governance","role:research-analyst","role:leadership","entity:data-source","state:connected","state:pending","state:not_started"],"sourceFiles":["lib/sources.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ingest_pipeline","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"Ingest Pipeline (lib/ingest)","description":"Central normalizer that every data path funnels into: API loads, CSV imports and connector results. Called as ingest(payload, how) with how ∈ api | csv | connector. Upserts metrics, snapshots, events and notes for a source/window into the store and records a synclog entry so the Data sources load history shows who/how/when data arrived. Throws errors with HTTP status for invalid payloads. (Implementation lives in lib/ingest.js, referenced from server.js.)","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","entity:metric","entity:snapshot","entity:event","entity:synclog","flow:data-load"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_source_lifecycle","type":"note","group":"group_catalog","data":{"text":"**State machine: data source status**\nnot_started → (account/access requested) → pending → (first successful load) → connected\n\n- Default state/note come from lib/sources.js\n- ingest() writes kind 'source' with state (payload.status.state or 'connected'), note, last_sync, window\n- Stored state overrides catalog defaults in the Data sources view\n- Example: PostHog catalog says 'pending' but seed/posthog.json sets status connected ('Project 347860, read by Research … 14 Oct')","color":"#fff8c5","sourceFiles":["lib/sources.js","lib/ingest.js","seed/posthog.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_connectors","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"Automatic Connectors (lib/connectors)","description":"Exports a map of connector functions (HubSpot, GA4, PostHog, Meta Ads, Clarity) and configured(key) which checks the source's service variables. Each connector pulls fresh data from the vendor API and returns an ingest payload. Used by both the scheduled autoSync and the manual Sync now endpoint. Sources without a connector (LinkedIn, Google Ads, Tag Manager) are fed via CSV or API.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","integration:posthog","integration:meta","integration:clarity"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_autosync","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"Scheduled Auto-Sync","description":"Background job in server.js that iterates all connectors, skips unconfigured ones, and ingests each result tagged 'connector'. First run 20 s after boot, then every 6 hours. Errors are logged to console per source and do not stop the others (failures here are not written to synclog, unlike manual sync). Keeps dashboard figures fresh without anyone pressing Sync now.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","tech:scheduler","flow:scheduled-sync"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_store_facade","type":"card","group":"group_storage","data":{"title":"Key-Value Store (MySQL or local JSON)","description":"A deliberately generic persistence layer so new sources and metric types need no schema migrations: every record is (kind, k, data JSON). Kinds: metric, snapshot, event, source, note, synclog. Interface: init, list(kind), upsert(kind,k,data), remove(kind,k), removePrefix(kind,prefix), count(kind), ping (used by /api/health). Chosen at startup: MySQL when DATABASE_URL, DB_HOST or MYSQL_HOST exists (Think4Ever runtime), otherwise data/local.json for local tests. list() returns data merged with _k (key) and _at (updated timestamp).","tags":["domain:persistence","tech:mysql","tech:json-file","entity:gd_item"],"sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"Seed Loader (seed/*.json)","description":"On first boot, loads bundled baseline data for each source that has no data yet — HubSpot and Google Analytics for 1–14 Oct 2026 — so the dashboard is populated immediately after deployment. Returns the number of sources seeded, logged at boot.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","flow:boot"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_store_mysql","type":"card","group":"group_storage","data":{"title":"MySQL Backend","description":"mysql2/promise pool (5 connections, utf8mb4, dateStrings) built from DATABASE_URL or DB_*/MYSQL_* variables. Creates gd_items on boot. Upsert uses INSERT … ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE on the unique (kind,k), making all loads idempotent. Parameterised queries prevent SQL injection; removePrefix escapes % and _ in LIKE patterns.","tags":["tech:mysql","integration:database","security:parameterised-queries"],"sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_csv_import","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"CSV Import (Data sources view)","description":"Lets Research upload metrics for sources without connectors (LinkedIn, Google Ads, Tag Manager, manual exports). CSV format: date, metric, value[, dim, dim_value]. The UI converts it to an ingest payload and posts to api/ingest with x-load-how: csv so loads appear as 'csv' in the load history.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","role:research","entity:metric","flow:csv-import"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_store_json","type":"card","group":"group_storage","data":{"title":"Local JSON Backend","description":"Fallback for developers running node _local.js without a database: holds {items:[{kind,k,data,at}]} in memory and rewrites data/local.json on every mutation. Same semantics as MySQL (upsert by kind+k). Not suited to concurrency or large volumes; data/ is excluded from the deploy zip.","tags":["tech:json-file","role:developer","env:local"],"sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_gd_items","type":"table","group":"group_storage","data":{"name":"gd_items","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"INT AUTO_INCREMENT","pk":true},{"name":"kind","type":"VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL"},{"name":"k","type":"VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL"},{"name":"data","type":"JSON NOT NULL"},{"name":"updated_at","type":"DATETIME ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP"}],"description":"Single physical table holding all dashboard data. UNIQUE(kind,k) is the business identity of each record; INDEX(kind) supports list-by-kind, the only read pattern (ordered by id). Logical entities by kind: metric (key source|metric|date|dim|dim_value), snapshot (source|key|from|to), event (source|date|timestamp|index), source (source id), note (note id), synclog (at|source).","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_entity_metric","type":"card","group":"group_data","data":{"title":"Entity: Daily Metric","description":"Atomic daily figure per source: { source, metric, date, value, dim?, dim_value? }. Examples: hubspot.sessions (dim_value = traffic source), posthog.ph_new_persons (dim_value 'Internal' marks staff accounts), ga4.ga_event (dim_value = event name like sign_up, form_start). Daily metrics follow the period selector and support previous-period comparisons and sparklines.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","entity:metric","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","integration:posthog"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_entity_snapshot","type":"card","group":"group_data","data":{"title":"Entity: Snapshot","description":"Table pulled for a fixed window that cannot be split by day: { source, key, from, to, rows[] }. Examples: ga4 'totals' (users, new_users, sessions, engaged_sessions, engagement_rate, avg_engagement_sec) and ga4 'events' (event, count, users). Rule: the UI picks the snapshot matching the selected period exactly, otherwise the one with the greatest overlap (ties: latest end, then longest), and always labels it with its own window.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","entity:snapshot","integration:ga4"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_kind_metric","type":"table","group":"group_storage","data":{"name":"kind=metric (daily fact)","columns":[{"name":"source","type":"string","pk":true},{"name":"metric","type":"string(60)","pk":true},{"name":"date","type":"YYYY-MM-DD","pk":true},{"name":"dim","type":"string(40)","pk":true},{"name":"dim_value","type":"string(120)","pk":true},{"name":"value","type":"number"}],"description":"Daily numeric facts powering time series: HubSpot sessions/new_visitors/pageviews/bounces/contacts by source; GA4 ga_sessions/ga_engaged_sessions/ga_users by channel and ga_event by event; PostHog ph_site_pageviews, ph_site_users, ph_cta_users, ph_registration_users, ph_portal_users, ph_new_persons (by type Internal/External), ph_event, ph_active_users; Meta ad_spend/impressions/clicks/results by campaign.","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js","lib/connectors.js","seed/hubspot.json","seed/posthog.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_entity_event","type":"card","group":"group_data","data":{"title":"Entity: Sign-up Event","description":"Individual record such as kind 'form_signup' from the HubSpot landing form with date and internal flag (email domain in INTERNAL_DOMAINS, default think4ever.com). Feeds the sign-up log, External vs Form sign-up KPIs and funnel step. Rule: when 'Exclude internal tests' is on, internal events are excluded from counts and shown muted in tables.","tags":["domain:conversion","entity:signup","integration:hubspot"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_kind_snapshot","type":"table","group":"group_storage","data":{"name":"kind=snapshot (window table)","columns":[{"name":"source","type":"string","pk":true},{"name":"key","type":"string(40)","pk":true},{"name":"from","type":"date","pk":true},{"name":"to","type":"date","pk":true},{"name":"rows","type":"array (≤500)"},{"name":"note","type":"string(300)"},{"name":"pulled_at","type":"ISO datetime"}],"description":"Pre-aggregated tables for a fixed window that cannot be summed from dailies: totals, countries, pages, utm_campaigns, forms, channels, events, new_people_by_source, live_insights, readings. Multiple windows per key coexist (e.g. GA4 totals for 1–14 Oct and for 7–14 Oct to show the post-test slowdown).","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js","seed/ga4.json","seed/hubspot.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_entity_note_source_log","type":"card","group":"group_data","data":{"title":"Entities: Timeline Note, Source Status, Sync Log","description":"Note { id, date, label, kind } annotates the timeline. Source { _k, state connected|pending|not_started, note, last_sync, window } tracks onboarding and freshness of each data source. Synclog { source, at, how api|csv|connector, error?, counts } is the audit trail of data loads (last 30 shown, newest first) in the Data sources view.","tags":["entity:note","entity:source","entity:synclog","domain:data-sources"],"sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_kind_event","type":"table","group":"group_storage","data":{"name":"kind=event (sign-up log)","columns":[{"name":"source","type":"string"},{"name":"kind","type":"string e.g. form_signup"},{"name":"date","type":"YYYY-MM-DD"},{"name":"form","type":"string"},{"name":"source_channel","type":"string (field 'source' in payload is overwritten by load source)"},{"name":"country","type":"string"},{"name":"internal","type":"boolean"},{"name":"domain_type","type":"none|internal|external"}],"description":"Individual conversion records (form sign-ups) without PII. Replaced per source per window on each load. Note: ingest spreads the event then sets source to the load source, so the event's attribution channel in the 'source' field is overwritten by 'hubspot' — a potential data-quality issue for the sign-up log's attribution column.","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js","lib/connectors.js","seed/hubspot.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"int_hubspot","type":"card","group":"group_integrations","data":{"title":"HubSpot","description":"Landing-page CMS/CRM. Provides landing sessions by traffic source, form sign-ups (contacts) and form data. Auth: HUBSPOT_TOKEN private app (contacts read, forms, business-intelligence). Primary source for the top of funnel and the sign-up log.","tags":["integration:hubspot","domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","entity:session","entity:signup"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"int_ga4","type":"card","group":"group_integrations","data":{"title":"Google Analytics 4 (+ Tag Manager events)","description":"Provides visitors, new users, engagement rate, engaged sessions, channels, UTM campaigns, countries and landing events (form_start, sign_up). Auth: GA4_PROPERTY_ID + GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT key JSON (Viewer). Data arrives as daily ga_event metrics or window snapshots.","tags":["integration:ga4","integration:google-tag-manager","domain:acquisition","domain:conversion"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_kind_ops","type":"table","group":"group_storage","data":{"name":"kind=source / note / synclog","columns":[{"name":"source.state","type":"connected|pending|not_started"},{"name":"source.note","type":"string"},{"name":"source.last_sync","type":"ISO datetime"},{"name":"source.window","type":"'from to to'"},{"name":"note.date/label/kind","type":"timeline note (test, other…)"},{"name":"synclog.source/at/how/metrics/snapshots/events","type":"load audit"}],"description":"Operational records: per-source live status overriding the catalog; timeline notes annotating the Overview sessions chart (e.g. tracking tests on 2 and 5 Oct); synclog audit of every load (how = seed, api, csv, connector) feeding the Data sources load history and the seed-once rule.","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js","lib/seed.js","seed/research.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"int_posthog","type":"card","group":"group_integrations","data":{"title":"PostHog","description":"Product analytics of the think4ever platform itself. Provides ph_new_persons (new people with an email = platform sign-ups from any entry point) with Internal flag, and activation. Auth: POSTHOG_HOST, POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID, POSTHOG_API_KEY. Until connected the UI shows 'Awaiting PostHog'.","tags":["integration:posthog","domain:conversion","entity:account"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"int_paid_social","type":"card","group":"group_integrations","data":{"title":"Meta Ads, LinkedIn, Google Ads, Clarity","description":"Social and paid channels plus UX behavior. Meta Ads (META_TOKEN, META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID) and Clarity (CLARITY_TOKEN) have automatic connectors; LinkedIn and Google Ads are loaded by CSV/API. Used in the Social and paid view to compute spend and cost per sign-up once campaigns run.","tags":["integration:meta-ads","integration:linkedin","integration:google-ads","integration:clarity","domain:paid-media"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","package.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed_hubspot","type":"card","group":"group_seed","data":{"title":"HubSpot Baseline (1–14 Oct)","description":"Research's manual pull from the HubSpot portal on 14 Oct. Daily sessions by source (Direct dominates; spikes on 2, 5, 6 Oct match tracking tests). Totals: 88 sessions, 35 visitors, 141 pageviews, 61% bounce, 12 contacts. Pages: go.think4ever.com/latam live (103 views, 69% bounce), go.think4ever.com/404 broken (37 views), hs-sites previews. UTM campaigns latam_launch_test and latam_lanzamiento flagged test:true. Countries led by Colombia (54 sessions). Forms: Landing Signup LATAM 12, Account Activity 10, platform #signupForm 2, #loginForm 3 — all internal (0 external); earlier site forms pre-launch had 14 external. 12 form_signup events, all internal, Colombia.","tags":["domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","integration:hubspot","entity:utm-campaign","entity:form","entity:page","data:seed"],"sourceFiles":["seed/hubspot.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"int_mysql","type":"card","group":"group_integrations","data":{"title":"MySQL (Think4Ever add-on) / local JSON","description":"Persistence via mysql2 using DATABASE_URL or DB_* variables; table gd_items created on boot. Without a database, data/local.json is used for local tests (node _local.js → localhost:3015).","tags":["integration:mysql","tech:mysql2","domain:storage"],"sourceFiles":["README.md","server.js","package.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed_ga4","type":"card","group":"group_seed","data":{"title":"GA4 Baseline (1–14 Oct)","description":"Snapshot-only baseline: totals 25 users, 59 sessions, 31 engaged (52.5%), 91 pageviews, 4 key events; second window 7–14 Oct shows only 7 users/12 sessions/0 key events (traffic stalled after tests). Landing events: generate_lead 9, sign_up 9, form_start 6, login 5 (4 users each — the testers). Channels (T4E Channels): Direct 37, Referral 8, Unassigned 7 (all 4 key events), Paid Social 5, Organic Social 2. Countries: Colombia 15 users, US 6, Canada 3, Bangladesh 1. Single page /latam (avg engagement 125s).","tags":["domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","integration:ga4","entity:channel","entity:landing-event","data:seed"],"sourceFiles":["seed/ga4.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_index_html","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Dashboard Shell (index.html)","description":"think4ever-branded single page: header with wordmark and 'LATAM Growth' title, global controls (Period: Since launch 1 Oct / Last 7 / 14 / 30 days / Custom date range; 'Exclude internal tests' toggle, checked by default; theme switch), and tabs Overview, Acquisition, Conversion, Social and paid, Data sources. Main area is rendered by app.js; footer and accessible toast (role=status) included. Loads Inter and Manrope from Google Fonts.","tags":["domain:dashboard-ui","role:research","role:marketing","tech:html"],"sourceFiles":["public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_app_state","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Client State & API Client (app.js)","description":"Global state S = { data, tab, period ('launch' default), from (LAUNCH 2026-10-01), to (today local), exInt (exclude internal) }. api() wraps fetch with JSON headers and the stored team code, intercepts 401 'code' to show the code prompt, and raises readable errors. Everything is fetched once from api/data and aggregated in the browser; relative URLs keep it working behind the /run/<id>/ proxy.","tags":["domain:dashboard-ui","tech:vanilla-js","entity:team-code","state:client"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed_posthog","type":"card","group":"group_seed","data":{"title":"PostHog Baseline (platform funnel)","description":"Read by Research from PostHog project 347860; sets source status to connected. Daily funnel metrics for think4ever.com/platform: site users, CTA users, registration users, portal users. Totals 1–14 Oct: 226 site users → 58 CTA → 27 registration starts → 84 portal users; 11 new external and 9 new internal people. Countries: US 127 site users but 0 external sign-ups; Colombia 32 users/15 CTA/9 reg/2 external; India 4 and Philippines 2 external sign-ups. new_people_by_source: Direct 4, think4ever.com 3, Google 2, LinkedIn 1, another workspace 1 — none external from the LATAM landing.","tags":["domain:activation","integration:posthog","entity:person","flow:funnel","data:seed"],"sourceFiles":["seed/posthog.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_seed_research","type":"card","group":"group_seed","data":{"title":"Research Readings Source","description":"A pseudo-source 'research' that carries the Research team's qualitative interpretation as a 'readings' snapshot (tone ok/warn/crit, title, text) displayed as the Overview 'research reading', plus timeline notes for the tracking tests on 2 Oct (landing form, 5 internal sign-ups) and 5 Oct (platform forms, 6 internal sign-ups). Shows that the ingest format doubles as a channel for human analysis, not just metrics.","tags":["domain:research","role:research-analyst","entity:reading","entity:timeline-note","data:seed"],"sourceFiles":["seed/research.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_aggregation","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Client Aggregation Engine","description":"Helpers that turn raw rows into business figures for the selected period: msum (sum a source/metric with filter and date range), has, byDay (daily series, optionally by dimension, zero-filled), byDim (ranked breakdown), snap (best snapshot for period), signups (form_signup events in range), phAccounts (PostHog new persons excluding Internal when needed), ga4Event (daily ga_event or snapshot fallback). Previous-period comparison uses an equal-length window right before 'from', only when the period starts after launch.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","entity:metric","entity:snapshot","entity:signup","tech:vanilla-js"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_readings","type":"card","group":"group_insights","data":{"title":"Launch Health Findings (14 Oct)","description":"OK: tracking works end to end — every test sign-up was attributed correctly in HubSpot and fired sign_up/login in GA4. OK: 11 external people signed up on the platform (2 from Colombia). WARN: no campaign is sending traffic — since 7 Oct 0–3 sessions/day, 0 sign-ups. WARN: the LATAM landing is not in the sign-up path — 'Sign up with Google' bypasses the HubSpot form; Colombia converts via think4ever.com instead. CRIT: 37 visits hit go.think4ever.com/404 — fix broken links before paid traffic to avoid paying for lost visits.","tags":["domain:research","role:leadership","role:growth-marketing","severity:crit","severity:warn"],"sourceFiles":["seed/research.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_kpi_strip","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Overview KPI Strip","description":"Six summary tiles: Landing sessions (HubSpot, sparkline + delta vs previous period), Visitors (GA4 users/new users/sessions), Engagement rate (GA4 engaged sessions, avg seconds), Sign-up submits (GA4 sign_up, includes internal tests), External/Form sign-ups (HubSpot form; tile turns red 'alert' when excluding internals yields zero), and Platform sign-ups (PostHog) or 'Awaiting PostHog'. Each tile carries a source tag showing connection state and data window.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","flow:overview","integration:hubspot","integration:ga4","integration:posthog"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","public/app.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_funnel","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Visit-to-Active-Account Funnel","description":"Core launch funnel across tools: Landing sessions (HubSpot) → Engaged sessions (GA4) → Started sign-up form (GA4 form_start users) → Submitted sign-up (GA4 sign_up users) → External/Form sign-ups (HubSpot form) → Platform sign-ups (PostHog, any entry point) → Activated. Missing steps render as striped 'pending' bars; conversion rates show between steps. Respects the Exclude internal tests toggle.","tags":["domain:conversion","flow:funnel","entity:signup","entity:account"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","public/app.css","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_growth_funnel","type":"note","group":"group_insights","data":{"text":"**Flow: LATAM growth funnel (visit → active account)**\n1. Acquisition: visitor reaches go.think4ever.com/latam via source/channel/UTM (HubSpot sessions, GA4 channels; Meta/LinkedIn/Google Ads spend)\n2. Landing engagement: scroll, form_start (GA4 via Tag Manager; Clarity UX)\n3. Sign-up: HubSpot form 'T4E – Landing Signup LATAM' → form_signup event; GA4 sign_up/generate_lead\n4. Platform: CTA click → registration → new person in PostHog (internal vs external by email domain)\n5. Activation: first project/build, portal use (PostHog)\n6. Cost per sign-up = ad_spend / sign-ups once campaigns run\n\n**Rule:** internal (think4ever.com) sign-ups excluded from growth counts\n**Baseline gap:** landing → platform link broken (Google sign-up bypasses form)","color":"#ffebe9","sourceFiles":["seed/research.json","seed/posthog.json","lib/connectors.js","lib/sources.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_api_ingest","from":"api_ingest","to":"node_ingest_engine","label":"submits external loads to","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_chart","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Daily Sessions Stacked Chart + Timeline Notes","description":"Hand-built SVG stacked bar chart of daily HubSpot sessions by traffic source, with nice-number gridlines, day totals, thinned date labels and a palette ordered by volume. Timeline notes in range are drawn as numbered orange dashed markers so the team can correlate spikes with launches, posts and fixes. Also small renderers: sparklines, horizontal bars with share %, tables, pills, empty states.","tags":["domain:growth-analytics","entity:note","tech:svg","flow:overview"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","public/app.css"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_ingest","from":"node_seed_loader","to":"node_ingest_engine","label":"loads baseline via","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_synclog","from":"node_seed_loader","to":"tbl_kind_ops","label":"checks load history to skip already-loaded sources","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_connectors_ingest","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_ingest_engine","label":"delivers pulled loads to","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_reg_hubspot","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_conn_hubspot","label":"gates & runs","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_views","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Dashboard Views (tabs)","description":"Overview: KPIs, funnel, research readings (ok/warn/crit/info callouts), daily sessions with notes. Acquisition: sessions by source (HubSpot), GA4 channels, UTM campaigns, countries. Conversion: landing events (GTM/GA4), sign-up log (internal rows muted), PostHog platform sign-ups, pages, forms. Social and paid: Meta, LinkedIn, Google Ads, Clarity and cost per sign-up. Data sources: status pills and editable state/notes, Sync now, CSV import, connection instructions, metric definitions, load history.","tags":["domain:dashboard-ui","domain:acquisition","domain:conversion","domain:paid-media","domain:data-sources","role:research","role:marketing"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.js","public/index.html","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_reg_ga4","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_conn_ga4","label":"gates & runs","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_reg_posthog","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_conn_posthog","label":"gates & runs","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_reg_meta","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_conn_meta","label":"gates & runs","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_reg_clarity","from":"node_connector_registry","to":"node_conn_clarity","label":"gates & runs","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_theme_css","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Brand Theme & Layout (app.css)","description":"think4ever design tokens shared with the Research Hub: navy for structure, orange as the single accent; semantic ok/warn/bad colors for status. Light/dark via prefers-color-scheme with manual override data-theme. Sticky header, responsive grids (6→3→2 KPI columns at 1100/820px), funnel, bars, charts, tables, forms, toast; reduced-motion and focus-visible accessibility.","tags":["domain:dashboard-ui","tech:css","tech:accessibility"],"sourceFiles":["public/app.css"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_ingest_store","from":"node_ingest_engine","to":"node_store_facade","label":"upserts facts, snapshots, events, status & audit into","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/ingest.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_store_mysql","from":"node_store_facade","to":"node_store_mysql","label":"uses in production","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_store_json","from":"node_store_facade","to":"node_store_json","label":"falls back to locally","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mysql_tbl","from":"node_store_mysql","to":"tbl_gd_items","label":"persists records in","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_tbl_metric","from":"tbl_gd_items","to":"tbl_kind_metric","label":"holds kind","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_boot","type":"note","group":"group_flows","data":{"text":"**Flow: Deploy & Boot**\n1. Operator uploads t4e-growth-dashboard.zip (no node_modules, data/, _local.js) as Node.js + MySQL project\n2. Start command `node server.js`; dependencies installed\n3. Server requires PORT, else exits(1)\n4. store.init() creates gd_items (or local JSON)\n5. seed() loads HubSpot + GA4 baseline (1–14 Oct 2026) for empty sources\n6. Listen; Think4Ever health check hits /api/health\n7. autoSync after 20 s, then every 6 h\n\n**Roles:** Operator/Research\n**Errors:** boot failure → exit(1); store down → health 503","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_tbl_snapshot","from":"tbl_gd_items","to":"tbl_kind_snapshot","label":"holds kind","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_tbl_event","from":"tbl_gd_items","to":"tbl_kind_event","label":"holds kind","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_tbl_ops","from":"tbl_gd_items","to":"tbl_kind_ops","label":"holds kind","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/store.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_hubspot_event","from":"node_conn_hubspot","to":"tbl_kind_event","label":"produces privacy-safe sign-up log","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_view_dashboard","type":"note","group":"group_flows","data":{"text":"**Flow: Team member reviews launch performance**\n1. Open dashboard → app.js calls GET api/data\n2. If TEAM_CODE set and missing → 401 'code' → Team code prompt → stored in localStorage → reload\n3. Choose period (since launch / 7 / 14 / 30 / custom) and Exclude internal tests\n4. Client aggregates metrics, picks best-overlapping snapshots, computes deltas vs previous equal window\n5. Read KPIs, funnel, readings, chart with timeline notes; switch tabs for detail\n\n**Roles:** Research, Marketing, Growth leadership\n**Rules:** internal domain sign-ups excluded when toggle on; snapshots labeled with their own window","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["public/app.js","public/index.html","server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_catalog_status","from":"tbl_kind_ops","to":"node_source_catalog","label":"live status overrides catalog state/note","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/sources.js","lib/ingest.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_catalog_connectors","from":"node_source_catalog","to":"node_connector_registry","label":"documents credentials required by","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/sources.js","lib/connectors.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_files_hubspot","from":"node_seed_hubspot","to":"node_seed_loader","label":"baseline file loaded by","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["seed/hubspot.json","lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_sync","type":"note","group":"group_flows","data":{"text":"**Flow: Connector sync (scheduled or Sync now)**\n1. Scheduler (6 h) or user clicks Sync now → POST /api/sync/:source\n2. Check connector exists (404) and service variables set (409)\n3. Connector calls vendor API (HubSpot/GA4/PostHog/Meta/Clarity)\n4. Payload → ingest(…, 'connector') → upsert metrics/snapshots/events + synclog\n5. On failure: synclog error entry (manual) and 502\n6. Data sources view shows last_sync and load history","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_files_ga4","from":"node_seed_ga4","to":"node_seed_loader","label":"baseline file loaded by","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["seed/ga4.json","lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_files_posthog","from":"node_seed_posthog","to":"node_seed_loader","label":"baseline file loaded by","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["seed/posthog.json","lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_seed_files_research","from":"node_seed_research","to":"node_seed_loader","label":"baseline file loaded by","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["seed/research.json","lib/seed.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_hubspot_seed_replaced","from":"node_conn_hubspot","to":"node_seed_hubspot","label":"supersedes baseline once configured","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js","seed/hubspot.json"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_manual_load","type":"note","group":"group_flows","data":{"text":"**Flow: Manual data load (CSV or API)**\n1. Research exports data from a source without connector (LinkedIn, Google Ads, GTM)\n2a. CSV in Data sources: `date, metric, value[, dim, dim_value]` → POST api/ingest with x-load-how: csv\n2b. Script: POST api/ingest { source, from, to, metrics, snapshots, events, notes } with x-ingest-key\n3. Server checks INGEST_KEY (401) → ingest() validates/upserts → synclog\n4. Dashboard reload shows new figures\n\n**Roles:** Research analyst, automation\n**Errors:** 401 key, 4xx validation","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["server.js","README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_ga4_seed_replaced","from":"node_conn_ga4","to":"node_seed_ga4","label":"supersedes baseline once configured","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js","seed/ga4.json"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_posthog_seed_replaced","from":"node_conn_posthog","to":"node_seed_posthog","label":"supersedes baseline once configured","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/connectors.js","seed/posthog.json"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_research_readings","from":"node_seed_research","to":"node_readings","label":"publishes findings","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["seed/research.json"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_notes_status","type":"note","group":"group_flows","data":{"text":"**Flow: Annotate timeline & track source onboarding**\n1. Add note (date, label, kind launch|content|fix|test|other) → POST /api/notes → 201\n2. Note appears as numbered orange marker on daily sessions chart; delete via DELETE /api/notes/:id\n3. Update source status (connected|pending|not_started + note ≤300) → PUT /api/sources/:key\n4. Status pills, source tags and empty-state texts update across views\n\n**Rules:** date regex, label ≤140, whitelists; unknown source → 404","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["server.js","public/app.js"]}}
